    "navBillions": null,
    "headline": "BCRED is a non-traded fund that lends money directly to private companies, mostly through senior secured, floating-rate loans, and passes the interest on to investors. Individual investors buy shares through a financial advisor at a price set each month, and can ask to sell back a limited amount each quarter."
  },
  "sectors": ["Software", "Healthcare", "Business Services", "Industrials", "Consumer", "Other"],
  "howItWorks": {
    "title": "How this fund works",
    "asOf": "2026-10-15",
    "paragraphs": [
      "The fund makes loans to private companies. Most are senior secured, meaning the fund is first in line to be repaid and the loan is backed by the company's assets, and floating rate, meaning the interest the fund earns moves with market rates.",
      "The share price (net asset value) is set once a month. Income is paid out as monthly distributions.",
      "Getting money out is limited by design. The fund offers to buy back shares each quarter, up to 5% of shares outstanding. If investors ask to sell more than that, requests are filled pro rata, so everyone gets the same fraction of what they asked for. Shares held for less than a year are bought back at 98% of their value.",
      "Each quarterly buyback is expected but not guaranteed. The board can change or pause the program."
    ],
    "source": {
      "name": "BCRED offering terms (bcred.com)",
      "url": "https://www.bcred.com/offering-terms/"
    }
  },
